codex
The format is now split into `physics/` and `views/`: physics records hold base/incumbent mappings, each unique candidate configuration’s current and three-offset profiles (network bits/joules, per-user attribution and served state, power/margin/ACM), plus per-row current/future geometry with provider-native elevation and true off-axis angle. Views hold the sealed 16/22 slots and exact/surrogate targets. I’m running a read-only four-step geometry smoke check before the six-hour clock starts.
