A concurrent legacy builder from the earlier attempt is still active in an isolated process namespace: its checkpoints appeared at 10:31 and 10:39 even though our process was stopped. Its old code uses a parent plus one anchor child, so I must count it as two Python processes. To honor the global cap, the repaired build will use one Python process until completion; it will write to a distinct staging namespace so the legacy job cannot delete or resume its checkpoints. This reduces width but should still fit all 180 anchors within the remaining budget.
